"""Chapter-specific openings, takeaways, and application questions."""
GUIDES={}
def add(n,raw):
    GUIDES[n]=[tuple(part.strip() for part in line.split(' || ')) for line in raw.strip().splitlines() if line.strip()]
    assert all(len(row)==3 for row in GUIDES[n]),n

add(2, '''Opening a feed looks like one action, but it can fetch many images and update several records. Begin by finding out what people need to do and which work each journey causes. || Count work at the boundary being designed, including operations caused by one user action. || Which requests and storage writes would a new image-upload feature add to the estimate?
Averages can make a slow service look healthy. Follow offered requests, completed work, individual waits, and errors to choose measurements that reflect what users receive. || Measure useful outcomes and their distribution, with an explicit population and observation window. || A service reports a low mean while some users wait a second. Which additional evidence would you request?
Suppose ten million people use the service daily. We will turn explicit activity assumptions into requests, stored bytes, transfer, and headroom, keeping each resource's calculation separate. || Workload estimates are inputs to capacity testing; per-instance capacity and failure needs require their own evidence. || If users view twice as many images but publish the same number of posts, which estimates change?
A queue grows even though all workers are busy. We will relate waiting, parallel work, and dependent calls before comparing the designs that could meet the requirements. || More concurrency helps only where work and resources permit it; compare feasible choices with their assumptions visible. || When would adding workers increase waiting instead of useful completions?''')
add(3, '''A browser has a website name, but packets need a destination and a transport. Trace how addresses, ports, sockets, and protocol behaviour connect the application to another machine. || Choose communication mechanisms by their actual delivery and ordering rules. || Where would you investigate if the application listens on its port but no remote client can reach it?
The first secure request is slower than the next, even with identical server work. Follow name lookup, setup, encryption, and connection reuse to account for the difference. || A request includes setup and travel as well as server execution; reused work changes the path. || Which parts of the 155 ms cold example can disappear with a usable warm connection?
A proxy, gateway, and balancer can all sit between a browser and an application. Assign each a purpose, then compare the work involved in polling and streaming updates. || Label the responsibility and trust of each intermediary rather than inferring behaviour from a product name. || Which policy belongs at the gateway, and which needs the service's knowledge of resource ownership?
The server commits, but the client receives no reply. Follow routing, discovery, caches, and bounded connection use to understand why a healthy destination does not guarantee a known result. || A timeout limits waiting; it does not identify whether remote execution occurred. || How would a client recover after losing the reply to a request that may have changed state?''')
add(4, '''A thousand uploads can wait on storage or compete for CPU. First identify the process, threads, memory, and resource ownership before selecting an execution model. || Match concurrency to the limiting resource and account for what remains alive while work waits. || Which resource changes first if uploads become CPU-heavy compression jobs?
One event-loop callback computes for two seconds while other tasks are ready. Trace readiness and execution to see how nonblocking I/O and bounded pools affect progress. || Overlapping tasks do not necessarily execute in parallel, and an event loop still needs short runnable turns. || Why can adding async tasks leave a CPU-bound loop unresponsive?
Two increments leave a counter at one. Trace each read and write, then choose a coordination boundary that covers the whole rule rather than only one assignment. || Protect the complete invariant at the actual shared-state boundary. || Which lock must both callers use, and why would separate per-caller locks fail?
A request ends while its child work still holds a large buffer and a connection. Connect publication, ownership, cancellation, and admission to keep shared state and resource use controlled. || Safe concurrent use includes visibility, lifetimes, and bounded waiting as well as individual state updates. || What must happen to local resources and required durable work when the parent request is cancelled?''')
add(5, '''One payment class checks orders, creates an SDK, and stores results. Divide the responsibilities, then examine which object relationships and contracts let those decisions change safely. || Organise payment rules and provider details so callers rely on meaningful behaviour. || Which part should change when the provider renames a field but the payment rule stays the same?
Two pieces of code look alike, but do they express the same rule? Apply design heuristics to actual changes instead of treating every repetition or method chain as a defect. || Share knowledge that has one meaning and owner; keep effects and intentions explicit. || When would merging similar validation code create a dependency between unrelated policies?
A payment keeps its identity while its status changes; a Money value is defined by its amount and currency. Use these differences to organise collaboration and test observable outcomes. || Keep identity, values, effects, and coordination distinct enough to reason about their changes. || Which checks can a fake gateway establish, and which require the real storage or provider boundary?
Refactoring a payment class should preserve approval, decline, and uncertainty. Follow those behaviours through structural changes and compare object-based and functional ways to express the decisions. || Improve structure while preserving the required outcomes and making external effects visible. || What regression test would catch a timeout accidentally being reclassified as a decline?''')
add(6, '''A notification service constructs its own provider and is difficult to test. Move that choice to startup, then distinguish supplying a dependency from choosing the interface policy relies on. || Injection supplies collaborators; inversion determines which abstractions and meanings the policy depends on. || Can a constructor receive an SDK while still exposing provider details throughout the service?
A background job uses a connection after its request scope has closed. Track creation, reuse, ownership, and disposal across the lifetimes involved. || A reference remains valid only under its resource's ownership and lifetime contract. || How should a job obtain resources if it must outlive the request that created it?
A service receives one container and resolves everything from it. Compare those hidden lookups with explicit collaborators and a narrow factory for legitimate runtime choices. || Use factories for creation decisions and explicit dependencies for work the caller already knows it needs. || What must a sender factory say about whether its returned object may be closed by the caller?
Creating a notification can require choosing a writer, a compatible family, or a valid combination of fields. These are different construction problems with different useful patterns. || Choose construction machinery for a real variation, and define validity and ownership of the result. || When would named constructor parameters be clearer than a builder?
A wrapper can translate an interface, add metrics, control access, or simplify a subsystem. Follow the intent and contract of each structural pattern to tell them apart. || Similar object diagrams can hide different purposes and different changes to behaviour. || Why does adding retries around a payment sender require more reasoning than adding timing metrics?
A changing algorithm, a lifecycle transition, and a request pipeline each vary for different reasons. Use behavioural patterns to place the right decision where it can evolve clearly. || Choose the extension point that matches the application's actual source of change. || How does choosing a pricing strategy differ from moving a payment into its next valid state?
A reservation update needs data access, eligibility checks, and a commit decision. Compare the patterns that make these responsibilities explicit without inventing a transaction across unrelated systems. || State which rule, model, and transaction each persistence pattern owns. || Which parts of a reservation and external payment can a local Unit of Work actually commit together?''')
add(7, '''A shopping application can separate input, policy, and storage without putting them on different machines. Compare architecture styles by their dependency rules and the changes they help contain. || Code boundaries and deployment boundaries solve related but different problems. || What benefit would justify turning a well-separated module into a remote service?
Catalog and fulfilment use different meanings for a product. Model those meanings with domain experts, then choose where rules need an atomic aggregate and which facts should become events. || A model is useful within a context whose vocabulary, ownership, and invariants are understood. || Which purchase-time facts should an order retain when the current catalog changes?
An order rule should not be rewritten in controllers, broker configuration, and provider adapters. Assign the business decision, its coordination, and its technical effects to clear owners. || Preserve domain meaning while translating transport, storage, and external models at explicit boundaries. || How would an anti-corruption layer handle a provider status whose name differs from your own model?
Five services always deploy together and share writable tables. Review whether the process split delivered independence, and use evidence to evolve toward a more manageable design. || Change architecture for demonstrated ownership, load, or failure needs while protecting existing properties. || When might consolidating services make the system easier to change and recover?''')
add(8, '''A client asks to create a payment. It needs a clear resource identity, valid amount representation, possible states, and bounded ways to read results. Build the contract before selecting request syntax. || An API describes behaviour and meaning as well as message shape. || Why can creating a payment resource succeed before the provider captures money?
A collection changes between pages, and a payment reply disappears before the client receives it. Use stable continuation and operation identities to give repeated calls a defined meaning. || Compatibility preserves meanings; cursors and idempotency keys need scope, validation, and recovery rules. || What should happen when an old idempotency key is reused with a different amount?
A signed-in client can still ask for another tenant's payment or overload an export. Combine access, resource limits, deadlines, and durable progress with clear acknowledgment boundaries. || Admission, permission, and completion answer different questions and need separate enforcement. || What can a webhook receiver acknowledge safely if its effect must survive a crash?
An event saved today may be replayed a year later. Keep schemas, consumer expectations, gateway roles, and documentation usable across that lifetime. || Supported consumers include delayed and recovering readers, not only today's newest client. || Which historical samples would you retain to check that a new decoder still supports recovery?''')
add(9, '''A ledger, profile, chat history, and search index do not make the same promises. Compare their reads, changes, and recovery needs before assigning a storage family. || Choose storage from operations and invariants, then verify the selected implementation's guarantees. || What would make a document model suitable for a profile but unsuitable for an unbounded chat history?
A PDF, a checkout row, and an analytical revenue scan read different shapes of data. Separate storage interfaces and physical layouts from the logical facts they represent. || Group bytes for the access pattern while preserving the meaning of current and historical facts. || Why should changing a customer's address leave the shipping address of an old order unchanged?
An order line refers to an order and a product, but those records have different lifecycles. Model keys, cardinalities, and ownership so data stays meaningful as it changes. || Relationships need both an expressed rule and a mechanism that preserves it. || What must happen to completed order history when a product is removed from sale?
Adding a search engine also adds another recovery and deletion path. Follow raw and derived copies through retention and operation before deciding that another store is worth maintaining. || Additional engines earn their cost through a demonstrated capability and a complete lifecycle. || How could restoring an old backup bring deleted content back into a search index?''')
add(10, '''A query finds a row through pages, indexes, memory, and storage. Follow that path to understand which physical work an index avoids and which costs remain. || Inspect the real plan and data distribution before changing indexes or hardware. || Why could an index that helps reads still reduce write throughput?
A reader sees an earlier row while a writer commits a new version. Connect transaction boundaries, logs, and visibility to explain both recovery and the observations readers may make. || Commitment, durable recovery, and snapshot visibility are distinct parts of the database contract. || Why does an engine using MVCC still need an explicit isolation policy?
Two buyers want one seat, while two doctors can jointly leave nobody on call. Trace the different conflicts and choose protection for the whole invariant. || Concurrency control must match the rule being preserved, not just the individual row being updated. || What does zero affected rows mean after an optimistic seat claim?
A pool is full and the backup job says it succeeded. Examine connection ownership, multi-statement transactions, and actual restore evidence before making a reliability claim. || Transaction scope and tested recovery must agree with the operation's promises. || Which check establishes that a restored booking database and its application are usable together?''')
add(11, '''A product is read repeatedly between edits. Work out which cost a cache can avoid, how much active data fits, and which layer should hold the reusable representation. || Cache value comes from useful reuse under a valid freshness and access policy. || Why can a high hit ratio coexist with slow or incorrect user responses?
A delayed reader inserts yesterday's price after a writer invalidates it. Follow cache population, expiry, versioning, and eviction as separate decisions. || Residence time and eviction policy do not by themselves establish current source data. || How can a one-minute TTL serve a value that is more than one minute behind its source?
A cache restarts just as a product becomes popular. Control duplicate loading, absent lookups, warming, and permitted stale results before the origin becomes overwhelmed. || Bound refresh and fallback work while keeping the accepted stale and absent meanings explicit. || What should happen if background refresh keeps failing past the allowed stale age?
A cache cluster and CDN add more copies and another failure path. Compare their operations with source correctness and recovery capacity, including whether the cache should exist at all. || Evaluate each cache by saved work, maintained semantics, and the cost of losing it. || Which workload would show that removing a cache improves the whole system?''')
add(12, '''Adding application instances changes traffic distribution and often connection demand. Find which work is independent, where required state lives, and which signal should drive growth. || Scale the constrained work while bounding shared downstream demand. || What must remain true before any healthy instance can serve the next request?
A dataset no longer fits its original owner. Compare copies, partitions, stable key placement, and ownership movement without assuming that evenly stored bytes imply evenly distributed traffic. || Data distribution needs query, invariant, routing, and migration rules as well as a key function. || Why does a new hash owner not automatically solve one extremely popular key?
A replica receives a write but has not applied it, while applications wait for connections. Follow actual progress and ownership before changing routing or increasing pool sizes. || Read freshness and capacity diagnosis depend on the real progress and wait boundaries. || How can doubling application replicas overload the same database?
The service needs more capacity and perhaps another region. Compare queues, failure placement, read and write rules, and total operating cost under equal requirements. || A bigger topology helps only when its capacity, authority, and failure behaviour match the need. || Which write invariant would remain concentrated despite adding many cold shards?''')
add(13, '''A client uploads bytes while the application records metadata. Make both identities and their handoff explicit so an interrupted transfer cannot become verified processing input. || Immutable content identity and a tracked lifecycle connect stored bytes to application progress. || What cleanup is needed if the object exists but its metadata transaction fails?
Search needs its own representation of source content. Follow term indexing, stage progress, and a generation switch while updates and deletions continue. || A derived index needs versions, access rules, and a rebuild protocol. || Why do matching document counts fail to prove that a reindex is ready to serve?
A nightly report and an immediate event alert need different freshness. Compare batch, continuous processing, transformation placement, and change capture using the progress each can establish. || Data movement needs a defined handoff, time meaning, and recovery position. || How should a late event change a result already published for a closed time window?
An extracted value is disputed after a pipeline update. Trace exact inputs, transformations, checks, and retained copies so the result can be investigated and corrected. || Quality and provenance belong to the output contract and every copy's lifecycle. || What would let an old worker recreate personal data after the source was deleted?''')
add(14, '''One service commits while its caller loses the reply. Begin with partial failures and the limits of time observations before trying to order events across machines. || A local observation may leave remote outcomes unknown; clocks describe different kinds of order. || Why does a missing heartbeat fail to prove that the old owner has stopped?
A user reads a value, writes another, and switches replicas. Describe the allowed observations before choosing a consistency model or relying on a product's “strong” label. || Choose consistency by legal histories and their scope. || Which history distinguishes a session moving backward from a permitted delayed read by another user?
A partition separates machines that all remain alive. Use CAP, ordinary coordination costs, and quorum intersection to identify what each side may safely do. || Set intersection supplies a protocol ingredient; authority and version rules supply the rest. || Which additional rules would a two-of-three read/write design need before claiming linearizability?
Some shared decisions need agreement; other work can proceed independently. State both forbidden outcomes and required progress, including the conditions under which progress can pause. || Safety and liveness are separate obligations under an explicit failure model. || How could a system preserve exclusive ownership while still failing every user's useful request?''')
add(15, '''A primary replies before a replica catches up. Compare replication models by write authority, acknowledgment milestones, conflicts, and the history available after failure. || Replica count matters only with persistence, ownership, and recovery rules. || What must a synchronous acknowledgment mean if it is meant to survive process loss?
A new leader must preserve accepted history. Study deterministic command application and the election, log, commit, and membership rules that make replicated decisions safe. || Consensus rules work together to preserve a decision history; a copy count is insufficient. || Why can an arbitrary old log entry on a majority still need more reasoning before commitment?
A paused worker wakes after its lease expired. Separate suspicion, ownership transfer, and resource-side enforcement to see where stale actions must be rejected. || Failure detection does not stop a process; the protected effect needs valid authority enforcement. || Where must token 7 be rejected after token 8 has become current?
Replicas must merge concurrent changes or choose which authority may proceed across regions. Evaluate convergence and recovery against the business invariant rather than as ends in themselves. || A deterministic merge is useful only when its meaning and failure assumptions fit the domain. || Why can a convergent counter still be unsuitable for allocating the last item?''')
add(16, '''A message is accepted, delivered, executed, and acknowledged at different times. Trace those boundaries to understand queues, logs, repetition, and the scope of delivery guarantees. || Name the accepted record or effect before claiming at-most-once, at-least-once, or exactly-once behaviour. || What changes if the consumer replaces its local counter update with an external email call?
A consumer crashes after applying an event, while another record fails on every retry. Design repeat-safe effects and a repair path, then distinguish delivery history from authoritative domain history. || Retrying, deduplicating, and preserving events serve different recovery needs. || How should a repaired poison record be replayed without duplicating its established effects?
An order commits but still needs publication and later compensation. Connect read models, outbox delivery, and sagas to make the obligations between local owners explicit. || Local atomic progress closes specific gaps while external steps retain their own failure and recovery rules. || Why can an outbox relay still publish one event twice?
A durable job outlives its request, scheduler, and first worker. Give each occurrence and attempt an identity, limit replay, and reconcile outcomes that remain uncertain. || Persistent ownership and safe effect identity let accepted work recover without inventing new intentions. || What should recovery do when a provider shows success but the local workflow remains pending?''')
add(17, '''Several replicas share a hidden dependency and fail together. Review the serving and data goals, then calculate what independent capacity really remains after a failure. || Redundancy requires independence, valid state, and sufficient surviving capacity. || Can two instances each at 70% load absorb the loss of either one?
A slow provider consumes every connection and triggers retries. Use deadlines, budgets, breakers, and resource isolation to limit the pressure rather than merely repeat the same work faster. || Bound both useful work and recovery attempts at the resource boundaries that can saturate. || Why can jitter reduce synchronisation while leaving total retry work excessive?
Some features can continue with reduced data; others must stop when their authority is unavailable. Define shedding, degradation, fallbacks, and probes from those meanings. || A degraded result must remain a permitted business outcome. || Why is a cached help page a different fallback from a guessed account balance?
The outage ends when useful service and required state recover. Set recovery objectives, test restores and authority changes, and learn from correlated failure rather than only process restarts. || Recovery evidence covers the tested journey and must account for unresolved business effects. || What could make a fast infrastructure recovery fail the original data-loss requirement?''')
add(18, '''A tenant administrator guesses another tenant's document ID. Follow identity, permissions, roles, and the trust boundaries the request crosses before deciding which controls are needed. || Authenticated identity is an input to resource-specific permission, not permission by itself. || Which paths must reject a tenant A administrator requesting tenant B data?
A stored file is encrypted, but the processing worker can read every file and every key. Examine credentials, cryptography, segmentation, and control placement against the actual threat. || Security depends on real access and key boundaries, including how they fail and rotate. || Which recovery assets become useless if their only decryption key is lost?
A correct API query is followed by a badly scoped cache or export. Carry tenant policy and minimal data through every copy, audit event, and deletion stage. || Isolation and privacy are lifecycle properties across the whole data path. || Which derived records could survive a delete that removes only the original file?
A trusted artifact still needs a controlled route to production, and users need workable safe recovery. Review the complete sensitive journey and the assumptions its controls depend on. || Secure design joins threat-specific controls with actual enforcement and testable outcomes. || What must happen if membership is revoked after a private export is queued?''')
add(19, '''A user waits while CPU looks normal. Combine population measurements, individual timelines, and structured events to find the work or wait the dashboard missed. || Useful telemetry connects a user-visible outcome to its resource and state path. || What can a trace show that a latency histogram cannot, and what can the histogram show that one trace cannot?
A full pool creates long waits, but paging on every CPU fluctuation overwhelms responders. Choose bounded evidence, indicators, and alerts that support a particular operating decision. || Measure the relevant denominator and make each urgent signal actionable. || Why should a unique request ID usually stay out of a general metric label?
A deployment precedes a slowdown, but correlation is only a clue. Use profiles, traces, query evidence, and a coordinated response to test explanations and restore useful service. || Separate triggers from mechanisms and preserve correctness while mitigating harm. || Which evidence would distinguish a slow query from a long wait to acquire its connection?
An asynchronous job remains unresolved after HTTP serving recovers. Follow the accepted operation through its later attempts, and use incident evidence to improve the system that owns it. || Operation age, outcomes, and recovery conditions extend beyond the original request. || What should an on-call engineer inspect when acceptance is healthy but document completion has stopped?''')
add(20, '''The same image works locally and fails in production. Compare environments and runtime isolation, keeping persistent state, resources, and platform duties explicit. || Packaging improves repeatability only with controlled configuration and appropriate state ownership. || Which data would disappear if a container's writable layer were replaced?
The scheduler cannot place new work, but existing requests still succeed. Separate control and serving paths, then examine startup, scaling, configuration, and replacement dependencies. || Running traffic and creating replacement capacity can depend on different paths. || Which dependency could let current instances serve while preventing every replacement from starting?
A release writes a new field, then a rollback restores a reader that cannot understand it. Keep artifacts, flags, configuration, and migration stages compatible while versions overlap. || Release safety includes data and protocol transitions, not only selecting an old executable. || At what point in expand-and-contract does rollback to the old reader become unsafe?
A managed platform offers useful capabilities while leaving application choices in your hands. Compare delegated work, limits, topologies, and internal developer needs under the same service requirements. || A platform abstraction should simplify repeated work while exposing the limits its users must manage. || Which correctness and recovery responsibilities remain with a team using a managed database?''')
add(21, '''A service misses its response-time goal. Budget the path, locate the limit, and design a benchmark that can test the proposed explanation without hiding waiting or errors. || Performance evidence is meaningful only with its workload, conditions, and outcome definition. || How could a load generator accidentally omit the very delays users would experience?
Extra nodes, caches, and transfer can change both capacity and cost. Compare complete architectures using explicit inputs and useful outcomes rather than one attractive infrastructure rate. || Filter by required behaviour before ranking cost, and keep modelled quantities distinct from measured results. || Why can a lower cost per attempt coexist with a higher cost per completed order?
An optimisation saves CPU while adding transfer, or a test suite adds checks without covering failures. Evaluate the whole effect and choose evidence for the particular risk. || Efficiency and validation should reduce real work or uncertainty without weakening the required contract. || Which failure window would a process kill before work begins leave untested?
A migration has matching row counts but wrong tenant ownership. Validate identities and invariants, preserve important regressions, and return to the requirements that justified the design. || Pair each requirement with evidence and keep unresolved targets clearly labelled. || What additional evidence would show that an equal-count migration preserved the right data?''')

CASE_OPENINGS={
1:'A short link hides a lookup, an ownership rule, and a cache-freshness decision. Follow one mapping from creation through redirect and revocation.',
2:'Three application instances each grant a full bucket of tokens. We need to decide whether the policy is local, globally strict, or a bounded allocation shared among regions.',
3:'A message can be safely stored while its live frame never reaches a device. Build chat around that distinction so reconnecting repairs delivery without creating another message.',
4:'The notification provider may accept a message just before its reply disappears. Track intent, attempts, and evidence so retries do not become unsupported delivery claims.',
5:'Preparing every follower feed makes reads cheaper but multiplies writes. Compare where the work belongs while keeping private and deleted posts out of every served page.',
6:'An encoder has written two of three required segments. Decide what makes the video ready, how a retry resumes, and which references a viewer is permitted to fetch.',
7:'Two riders select the same nearby driver. Spatial search can find candidates; an authoritative claim must decide who actually receives the assignment.',
8:'A payment succeeds just after a seat hold expires. Follow the reservation, current seat owner, and provider evidence to find an outcome that does not sell the seat twice.',
9:'A provider charges successfully, but the local service stops before recording the reply. Use stable identity and reconciliation to connect the external result to one valid local posting set.',
10:'A scheduler and its worker can both restart around a due job. Give the schedule, occurrence, attempt, and effect separate identities so recovery knows what it is resuming.',
11:'Two collaborators insert text at the same position and receive the edits in different orders. The editing protocol must define a shared interpretation and preserve the context needed to reconnect.',
12:'A document can finish extraction yet still need review, publication, or deletion. Model the whole lifecycle so each result is usable, authorised, and traceable to its input.'}

CASE_CAPTIONS={
1:['A link has one owner and a unique code. The stored operation identifies its creation result.','Creation and redirect use authoritative mappings; analytics is a separate obligation.','Test a collision, a lost reply, and a stale cached target at their different boundaries.','Add capacity for a measured limit while preserving code uniqueness and revocation.'],
2:['A bucket groups scope, policy, tokens, and refill time in one coordinated record.','Derive trusted scope before making the refill-and-spend decision.','Two callers must not independently spend the same last token.','Move from local to shared admission only with an explicit scope and allocation rule.'],
3:['History, membership, and receipt progress have different owners and lifetimes.','Store the message before reporting persistence, then deliver and recover by identity.','A missed live frame is recovered from history; repeating a send retains its original identity.','Scale connections and fan-out without losing per-conversation progress.'],
4:['Intent, delivery tasks, attempts, and callbacks record different stages of the notification.','Durable intent reaches a bounded channel worker and a provider with explicit outcome meanings.','A sent message with a lost reply is uncertain, so recovery needs provider evidence or a stated duplicate policy.','Add channels and routes after defining their expiry, priority, and retry behaviour.'],
5:['The post and access relationships are authoritative; feed candidates are derived references.','Combine candidates, enforce visibility, rank, and return a bounded page.','Repeated fan-out and stale candidates must not create duplicate or forbidden visible posts.','Prepare common feeds only where measured reading saves more work than publication adds.'],
6:['A published manifest generation names identified, verified outputs from a particular input and profile.','Uploaded bytes become playable only after required transformation and publication checks.','Partial segment output stays unpublished until the required generation is complete.','Scale encoding separately from delivery and preserve versioned playable sets.'],
7:['Latest position helps search; driver and trip state decide exclusive assignment.','Candidate search precedes a valid conditional offer acceptance.','Two riders can choose one candidate, but only one authoritative claim may win.','Partition location work without creating conflicting assignment owners.'],
8:['Seat, hold, payment, and ticket records must preserve their defined ownership relationships.','A hold and payment workflow lead to a version-checked confirmation or supported recovery.','An old expiry or late payment must not overwrite a newer seat owner.','Add admission and partition independent events while protecting the same seat invariant.'],
9:['Operation identity links provider evidence to payment state and balanced accounting entries.','Persist intent, obtain or reconcile provider evidence, and commit the required local result.','A lost provider reply leaves uncertainty rather than proof that no charge occurred.','Scale useful independent work while keeping each prior operation and posting explainable.'],
10:['One scheduled occurrence can have several attempts, while retaining one logical run identity.','Create due work durably before a current worker attempts its effect.','A replaced worker can resume, so its stale completion must be rejected at the protected boundary.','Separate scan capacity from execution while preserving occurrence and effect identities.'],
11:['Operations, snapshots, and retained context describe the same document history under one protocol.','Local edits become accepted operations and reconnectable history through explicit sync rules.','Concurrent or repeated operations need deterministic interpretation and stable identity.','Distribute documents and compact history only within the supported offline and merge contract.'],
12:['Fields and decisions retain tenant, input, transform, and evidence relationships.','Ingestion, extraction, review, and publication have distinct durable progress.','A stale attempt cannot publish after its authority or document has been withdrawn.','Scale stages independently while retaining provenance, access, and deletion behaviour.']}
